            {
                "entry_id": "c863c9d1-6bf1-38f5-a901-568aaf763ae7",
                "word": "scolopendre",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "f1ca61a0-6d0b-4506-b3d8-1aded74d9012",
                        "entry_id": "c863c9d1-6bf1-38f5-a901-568aaf763ae7",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "scolopendres"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4b49176c-f2a8-3e48-a18f-26190bff05e9",
                        "entry_id": "c863c9d1-6bf1-38f5-a901-568aaf763ae7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Genre de myriapodes, au corps long et très étroit, et qui vivent sous les pierres, dans le bois pourri, etc."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Arthropodologie"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ea756312-13fe-414e-a1ad-fe1e2f752f62",
                                "sense_id": "4b49176c-f2a8-3e48-a18f-26190bff05e9",
                                "text": "Ariſtote dit qu’en couppant une ſcolopendre en deux, l’une des parties ira en avant, & l’autre en arriere : c’eſt pourquoy Nicander dit auſſi qu’elle a deux teſtes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c48d7d29-321c-4685-9ba6-b876edb86808",
                                "sense_id": "4b49176c-f2a8-3e48-a18f-26190bff05e9",
                                "text": "Cela a fait naître un ſoupçon à quelques Savants, qui ont teimoignè, qu’il ſeroit bien-aiſe, ſi on voudroit bien obſerver, ſi notre Scolopendre marine luiſante, ne fût peûtetre pas de cette eſpèce d’Insectes marins […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3e492e49-0fd4-4452-a70f-4fcac352e1e0",
                                "sense_id": "4b49176c-f2a8-3e48-a18f-26190bff05e9",
                                "text": "Une scolopendre d’une vingtaine de centimètres avait enfoncé ses deux crochets dans la peau."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0b09b4b3-d6d3-4ce4-aa6f-14c8673ffa52",
                        "source_entry_id": "c863c9d1-6bf1-38f5-a901-568aaf763ae7",
                        "source_sense_id": "4b49176c-f2a8-3e48-a18f-26190bff05e9",
                        "target_lang_word": "centipede",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "centipede",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "56fbf60b-b6b8-30e2-bcd8-66bca7bf2dcc",
                                        "entry_id": "4e9afd66-0b9a-3a59-a21b-dc308533c030",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any arthropod of class Chilopoda, which have a segmented body with one pair of legs per segment and from about 20 to 300 legs in total."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4374c3fb-5dba-480a-b4ab-17f20ac3ece1",
                                                "sense_id": "56fbf60b-b6b8-30e2-bcd8-66bca7bf2dcc",
                                                "text": "Centipedes differ from millipedes by having a single pair of legs on each body segment."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "96686866-bb91-476d-8614-ac4c115e709b",
                                                "sense_id": "56fbf60b-b6b8-30e2-bcd8-66bca7bf2dcc",
                                                "text": "The existence of millipedes, centipedes, insects, and spiders along-side the first tetrapods sustained a robust ecosystem in which most animals were predators or scavengers."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "30ad95fa-d7c9-4868-aaff-4d6249ef810a",
                                                "sense_id": "56fbf60b-b6b8-30e2-bcd8-66bca7bf2dcc",
                                                "text": "All centipedes (Chilopoda) and spiders (Aranea) are predatory and although they are often found on corpses their impact on the other fauna is not known."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9bfa6b51-06ed-3ac0-951a-91d9272d4b90",
                                        "entry_id": "4e9afd66-0b9a-3a59-a21b-dc308533c030",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A many-oared Chinese smuggling boat."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
